think Designed the exact primitive: every hull vertex is one of contour's ring pixels (the hull was built from the ring), so consecutive hull vertices in ring order bound a run of boundary pixels; for each hull edge the defect is the run pixel of greatest |cross(A,B,P)| (twice the triangle area, exact i64), and a straight edge (every cross zero) carries no dent. The DEEPEST defect is chosen across edges by an EXACT i128 cross-multiplication -- depth_i > depth_j iff cross_i^2 * len_j > cross_j^2 * len_i, the square roots cleared by squaring, the same discipline min_area_rect selects its supporting edge by; only the reported depth is read in f64.
think Designed the decisive crux before coding as two facts: a COUNT crux over rasters (a convex block reads zero defects, an L one, a plus four -- the point-by-point concavity a single solidity number blurs), and a DEPTH crux as pure integer point sets (a shallow dent depth 3 on a long chord length 10 raw cross 30, a deeper dent depth 4 on a short chord length 5 raw cross 20 -- the naive raw-cross argmax picks the shallow dent 30>20, yet the exact i128 comparison 30^2*25=22500 < 20^2*100=40000 names the deeper one, disagreeing with the float-free naive read).
obs GREEN on the FIRST metal run -- every crux held as designed: block 0 defects, L exactly 1, plus 4, and the exact-i128 selection returned the right dent against its own larger-raw-cross sibling. Measurement confirmed the raster counts I reasoned rather than guessed (block/L/plus = 0/1/4).
obs TAME gate caught two compound asserts in deeper_than (`ci >= 0 and cj >= 0`, `li >= 1 and lj >= 1`) -- split each into named single asserts so a failing half names itself; tame_style_check then GREEN, width-check exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII.
obs The decisive-depth crux is the Lindy heart of the rung: holding the exact (cross_area, chord_len_sq) pair and comparing in i128 makes the deeper dent a tolerance-free arithmetic fact, so the selection can never be wrong by a float rounding -- the same choice min_area_rect made for its supporting edge, and moments for its orientation-in-f64-report-only stance.
